  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inter-European Noncommissioned Officer Academy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This course is a modified version of the USAF Noncommissioned Officers Academy course which prepares NCOs for more advanced leadership and management responsibilities. It is the next level of PME designed for those assuming senior NCO leadership positions. Students learn time and stress management, concepts of human behavior, teambuilding, critical thinking, effective communication, and leadership techniques, as well as implementing quality in the workplace. Experiential course activities challenge each student to apply curriculum concepts successfully and to influence group dynamics, cohesion, and effectiveness in a positive manner. By virtue of its international student body, IENCOA fosters positive relationships between NATO and PfP members, as well as expanding students cultural knowledge and learning in a manner consistent with U.S. and NATO objectives. This course is delivered in parallel with the Inter-European Squadron Officer School to highlight the benefit of a professional officer and NCO corps relationship and develop an understanding of the importance of delegating authority and responsibility for operationally effective high-tempo aviation operations and support.</narrative>
  </description>
